a} = \\text{Area of } \\triangle BKL + \\text{Area of } \\triangle BCL\n\\]\n\nGiven the symmetry and the distances, we can find that:\n\\[\n\\text{Area} = 784 \\sqrt{3}\n\\]\n\n### Step 8: Identify \\( n \\)\nThe area is expressed as \\( n \\sqrt{3} \\), so:\n\\[\nn = 784\n\\]\n\n### Final Answer\n\\[\n\\boxed{784}\n\\]",
